    "Fold of dCamera_c: 16 named members plus 37 camera state handlers/dispatchers recovered as unmangled func_* symbols. mwccarm emits .text in reverse source order, so the file runs ROM-descending from classInit. The recovered bodies were C; each sits under `#pragma cplusplus off` (the pinned -lang c++ build parses those regions as C89, so block-top declarations only) keeping the unmangled symbol names.",
    "Leftovers: the C bodies keep raw-offset member access ((char*)self + 0xNNN) where the real field names are not yet recovered, and the camera state records are TU-local opaque typedefs (CamEntryE, CamFixedTab, CamViewObj, CamStateBase, CamStateIdx, CamJitter, the dBgCh_* shadows). POD `Vec3` shadows replace Vector3 inside the C regions because Vector3's empty destructor makes it non-POD and inflates the stack frame by 8 bytes (measured on func_0200c394).",
    "The 88 functions below 0x0200bec4 were one-function shards (66 C, 20 C++); they now use dCamera_c/dActor_c/Player member names in C++ under extern \"C\" (no cplusplus-off regions), share the file's CamMode/CamViewObj/Entry3 records, and keep their ROM names."
